{!Today}

Dear {!Contact.FirstName},

The {!Organization.Name} is honored by your desire to become a Blood Program Leader. I am a local representative here at the Red Cross and will be working closely to identify the best partnership opportunity.  As you may imagine, COVID-19 is having a significant impact on our operations, so I hope you’ll forgive my outreach via email so that I can be more responsive.  I look forward to continued conversations to get to know you better as we begin our work.  One of the things we can make progress with quickly is establishing what your service will look like. Here’s what the most successful blood drive hosts prepare to deliver:
 
A suitable site: An indoor space with a minimum of 1,000sq ft and 6 outlets is ideal for donor comfort, and COVID-19 precautions like social distancing are currently required. If you do not have an indoor space, we can discuss bringing a bloodmobile. Let me know what kind of space parameters you might have available for blood drives.

A recruitment plan: A successful blood drive is built on getting the word out to as many people as possible and filling a drive day schedule. Social media, email and phone are all important, but the #1 way to recruit a blood donor is by asking them face-to-face (and, of course, we’ll be planning well beyond the current public health challenges).

A recruitment team: The American Red Cross will support you with tools, tips and tricks honed over 75 years. In addition, you’ll need a team of people you trust to help you recruit blood donors and support smooth operation on Drive Day.

Willing donors: A minimum of 25 donors, that means a donor pool of at least 250 people since typically 10% are willing to donate.  Attached is an interest survey where you can begin fielding donors. Would you be willing to gauge interest and send me your findings for planning purposes?

Flexibility to support greatest need: Even beyond unique challenges like COVID-19, there are always challenges to blood collection including inclement weather, local disasters, and seasonal illness. In effort to sustain consistent blood collection, we appreciate your flexibility of potentially hosting in the short future or over the next several months.  Please let me know your ideal time-frame for hosting blood drives.

In closing, with your insights, we can get started building a blood drive program, and community service, of which you can be proud. On behalf of patients in need, and those who love them, thank you for your commitment to their care. 

Sincerely,
{!User.FullName}
{!Organization.Name}
{!User.Email}

P.S. If you’re uncertain about aspects of sponsorship and initially prefer to discuss via phone, please let me know and I will schedule a time.